# Animation_App Architecture Rules

The human-readable architecture specification is `docs/architecture.md`;
the data model is `docs/data-model.md`; the file format is
`docs/project-file-format.md`; decisions are in `docs/decisions.md`. The
condensed rule set that every agent reads is `AGENTS.md` at the root.

## 1. Layers and dependency direction

```text
src/domain   pure TypeScript: types, schema, transforms, animation
             evaluation, migrations. No DOM, no React, no browser APIs.
src/app      commands, ProjectStore (undo/redo), editor state, playback.
             Depends on domain only.
src/render   Canvas 2D renderer, image cache, hit testing.
             Depends on domain only.
src/infra    IndexedDB, .animproj files, image decoding, video export.
             Depends on domain only.
src/ui       React components. May depend on all of the above.
```

Never import from `ui` into any other layer. Never import a browser API
into `domain` or `app`; their tests run in Node and will fail if you do.

## 2. Source of truth

The `Project` value held by the store is the only source of truth. Do not
keep a second copy of scene, character or animation data in a component,
the canvas, or a library's scene graph. Editor state (selection, playhead,
zoom) is separate and is never saved to the project file.

## 3. Commands

Every change to the project goes through `store.dispatch(name, draft =>
…)`. Never mutate the project elsewhere. Continuous gestures use
`store.transient` and commit one `dispatch` at the end.

## 4. Rendering

One renderer function serves the viewport, playback and export. Do not add
a preview-only or export-only drawing path. Overlays (handles, pivots,
selection) are drawn on a separate canvas.

## 5. Persistent data

The file format is user data. Changing `docs/data-model.md`,
`docs/project-file-format.md`, the zod schema or the IndexedDB layout
requires an ADR, a `formatVersion` bump where the rules in
`docs/project-file-format.md` §4 say so, and migration tests.

## 6. Dependencies

The runtime dependency list is fixed in `docs/architecture.md` §2. Adding
one requires an ADR and a sentence in the pull request explaining why the
existing tools are insufficient.

## 7. Architectural changes require review

If the current architecture prevents a required feature from being
implemented correctly: explain the limitation, describe the proposed
change, identify affected components, documentation and tests, and ask for
approval before making it. Small decisions inside the documented
architecture do not require approval.
